insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('739510ef-f3ce-5989-9336-c22d735624fe', 'rg5-context-clues-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-context-clues'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Masters of Disguise$q$, $q$The octopus is one of the ocean's most amazing animals. It has no bones, so its soft body is very flexible. An octopus can bend and squeeze through a hole no bigger than a coin.

An octopus is also a master of camouflage. Camouflage is a way of hiding by blending in with the surroundings. Its skin holds thousands of tiny color cells. In less than a second, an octopus can turn from red to sandy brown to match the sea floor.

This skill helps the octopus stay safe from predators, the animals that hunt and eat it. Sharks, eels, and large fish all search the reef for a meal. If the octopus is spotted, it has another trick. It squirts a cloud of dark ink. The ink makes the water murky, so the hunter cannot see clearly. While the predator is confused, the octopus darts away.

Scientists also say octopuses are curious. In aquariums, they explore new objects, poke at them, and even open jars to see what is inside.$q$, 'draft')
